# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Table Mountain POV - ignored paths
#
# Rationale: this repo holds a 2.3 GB working set, almost all of it source or
# derived geospatial binaries. None of it belongs in git history. What IS
# tracked is the reproducible definition of the project: docs, scripts, the
# QGIS project, the Processing models, and the config files they need.
# data/ is empty in git: `just fetch-sources` downloads the OSM PBF and
# contour archive, then `just rebuild-all` creates every GIS derivative.
# Every ignored path below is either source data held locally or regenerable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.bck
data/
.claude/worktrees

# --- Python environment and tooling ---------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- SQLite WAL journal sidecars ------------------------------------------
# Opening a GeoPackage in QGIS (or any SQLite client) can leave -wal/-shm
# companions or touch the header; the database content is the source of truth.
*.gpkg-wal
*.gpkg-shm
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm

# --- Editor / OS noise ----------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- data/ ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing under data/ is tracked. `just fetch-sources` downloads the Geofabrik
# PBF and CoCT contour ZIP. Unzip the contour archive before `just rebuild-all`;
# the Shapefile set and every generated GeoPackage, raster, overview, diagnostic,
# and provenance file remain local. Private audit inputs and local notes are
# local-only too.
#
# Git does not descend into an ignored directory, so data README files are local
# documentation and cannot be re-included by the global !**/README.md guard.
data/

# --- Blender scene backups ------------------------------------------------
# Blender writes a .blend1 auto-backup beside each .blend on every save.
# Backups are regenerable by definition and were never intended to be tracked.
blender/*.blend1

# NOTE: blender/*.blend is deliberately NOT ignored. The README treats scenes as
# build outputs, but scripts/blender/ does not exist, so the current .blend
# files are not reproducible from this repo. Track them until a build script
# exists; add an ignore rule at that point, not before.

# --- QGIS project save side-files -----------------------------------------
# QGIS >= 3.22 writes a <name>.qgs~ backup and a <name>_attachments.zip beside
# the project file on every GUI save. Neither is disableable and both are
# regenerable, so they are never committed; the tracked .qgs is always the
# build output (see qgis/README.md). The generic `*~` and `*.zip` rules above
# already matched these; the explicit rules document the intent.
*.qgs~
*_attachments.zip

# --- Render output --------------------------------------------------------
# Blender frames and videos; the directory stays present but empty in git.
renders/*

# --- Caches ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Temporary files only; safe to clear at any time.
cache/*

# --- MapProxy runtime output ---------------------------------------------
# Both rules ignore directory CONTENTS, never the directory itself, so the
# directory stays tracked and !**/README.md below remains effective.

# Tile cache. One SQLite level database per zoom level, regenerable by
# `just seed-mapproxy` or on demand. config/mapproxy.yaml is the source of
# truth for what goes in here.
docker-mapproxy/cache_data/*

# MapProxy log output. The directory is tracked (via .gitkeep) because Docker
# creates a missing bind-mount source as root:root, which uid 1000 could not
# write to. The log files themselves are transient.
docker-mapproxy/logs/*
!docker-mapproxy/logs/.gitkeep

# Artifacts the image writes into the config directory on every start. The two
# yaml files there are the source of truth and stay tracked.
#   log_*.ini        copy of settings/log.ini, referenced by the generated app.py
#   default_path.txt records the cache dir between starts
#   *_mapproxy.log   zero-byte placeholders, see the LOGGING comment in compose
docker-mapproxy/config/log_*.ini
docker-mapproxy/config/default_path.txt
docker-mapproxy/config/*_mapproxy.log

# The demo page rendered by the nginx container. web/index.html.bck is the
# source of truth: web/nginx_conf.sh runs
#   envsubst < /web/index.html.bck > /web/index.html
# on every start, substituting the OWS endpoint built from NGINX_HOST and
# MULTI_MAPPROXY. The output is container output, is written as root, and is
# regenerated on each start, so it is not tracked. An earlier commit had
# captured a rendered copy with a then-current endpoint baked in.
docker-mapproxy/web/index.html

# --- Keep the provenance READMEs even inside ignored directories ----------
# Re-includes READMEs that the broad `dir/*` rules above would swallow
# (renders/, cache/, docker-mapproxy/). It deliberately cannot reach anything
# under data/: that directory is ignored as a whole, so data/README.md stays
# out of git and its content lives in REPRODUCTION.md.
!**/README.md
# CocoIndex Code (ccc)
/.cocoindex_code/
